{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73031,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3c802bb66af563aaaa80cc2a3054839c","RawContent":"I will send you the price list Mayte sent me last week. I have done ton of research on photographers. My favorite In terms of quality\/quantity of time and pictures in packages\/ and affordability -Caribbean Emotions -Huellas del Caribe -Photosouvenir They all do videography as well. I love the pictures of both CE and HDC but I think HDC has more tasteful videography in terms of editing and such just based on only what I have seen. However, I want to go with photosouvenir for the trash the dress session because they have an option where they take you to a lagoon to shoot underwater!! Price range for that is steep in comparison to a regular trash the dress but the pictures are so unique! I think katya nova does this too but with her prices i&#039;d have to limit myself too much... [quote name=\"jeabeeW\"]\nHi All! I&#039;m new as well and messaged Mayte recently for wedding info. I have done a TON of research on this site as well as others regarding Jellyfish. Each list prices from different years. Could someone please send me the most recent price list? I&#039;d greatly appreciate it! jbrooke.wooddell@gmail.com I also want opinions on photographer cost. I have a great photographer from home whom I&#039;m willing to fly out.  Her cost is $1600 + flight and room. She has done a photo shoot with us before. We have mutual friends so she somewhat knows our personalities. We would have her form the entire wedding day, + the pay prior at the resort. I thinks this is a GREAT deal but the fianc\u00a9 is questioning if we can find cheaper in PC. I love Katya Nova&#039;s work $2800 (starting) but this is for two photographers I think (her&amp; her hubby). Total cost is relatively the same so here is the issue... -1 photographer vs. 2 -2photgrathers for 1 day vs. 1 photographer for a few days -More pics during the wedding vs. more candid&#039;s over the course of the trip. what would you all do??? We are also considering adding a videographer. Any suggestions of good\/affordable work? I want the trailer style. Also, I have not reached out to Kayta, if any of you have used her &amp; Rob, plz give me some insight on what is included in the $2800. Last thing, If JF is booked, I&#039;m looking at Huracan Caf\u00a9 as an option. Anyone look into that venue? I have seen pic from one wedding. Sry sooooo many questions. :)[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1804294,"PostDate":1380654519,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I will send you the price list Mayte sent me last week. I have done ton of research on photographers. My favorite In terms of quality\/quantity of time and pictures in packages\/ and affordability -Caribbean Emotions -Huellas del Caribe -Photosouvenir They all do videography as well. I love the pictures of both CE and HDC but I think HDC has more tasteful videography in terms of editing and such just based on only what I have seen. However, I want to go with photosouvenir for the trash the dress session because they have an option where they take you to a lagoon to shoot underwater!! Price range for that is steep in comparison to a regular trash the dress but the pictures are so unique! I think katya nova does this too but with her prices i'd have to limit myself too much... <blockquote class='ipsBlockquote' data-author=\"jeabeeW\" url=\"\/t\/85319\/total&#045;cost&#045;of&#045;wedding&#045;at&#045;jellyfish&#045;punta&#045;cana\/30#post_1947226\"><p>Hi All! I'm new as well and messaged Mayte recently for wedding info. I have done a\u00a0TON of research on this site as well as others regarding Jellyfish. Each list prices from different years. Could someone please send me the most recent price list? I'd greatly appreciate it! jbrooke.wooddell@gmail.com I also want opinions on\u00a0photographer cost. I have a great photographer from home whom I'm willing to fly out.\u00a0\u00a0Her cost is $1600 + flight and room. She has done a photo shoot with us before. We have mutual friends so she somewhat knows our personalities. We would have her form the entire wedding day, + the pay prior at the resort. I thinks this is a GREAT deal but the fianc\u00a9 is questioning if we can find cheaper in PC. I love Katya Nova's work $2800 (starting) but this is for two photographers I think (her& her hubby). Total cost is relatively the same so here is the issue... -1 photographer vs. 2 -2photgrathers for 1 day vs. 1 photographer for a few days -More pics during the wedding vs. more candid's over the course of the trip. what would you all do??? We are also considering adding a videographer. Any suggestions of good\/affordable work? I want the trailer style. Also, I have not reached out to Kayta, if any of you have used her & Rob, plz give me some insight on what is included in the $2800. Last thing, If JF is booked, I'm looking at Huracan Caf\u00a9 as an option. Anyone look into that venue? I have seen pic from one wedding. Sry sooooo many questions. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p><\/blockquote>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rocioechev@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"98.249.170.155","